' school_lock.rr: School Lock as RapidR Studio sees it on this computer —
' for a school's IT, to check the policy file after writing it, and for
' anyone curious how hard a password is to guess
' (docs/manual/for-teachers.md).
'
'   rapidr run school_lock.rr
'
' RProject's SchoolLock members are the ones Studio uses: SchoolLockLoad
' reads the computer's policy (and a user's own setting, here none),
' SchoolLock("…") says what is locked, SchoolLockStrength how hard a
' password is to guess (0 too short … 3 strong). Nothing is changed here:
' a teacher turns the lock on in Studio (Tools > School Lock…), IT with
' the policy file.

DIM Studio AS RProject
DIM Locked AS INTEGER
DIM Words(4) AS STRING
DIM Names(3) AS STRING
DIM k AS INTEGER

PRINT "School Lock as RapidR Studio sees it:"
Locked = Studio.SchoolLockLoad("")
IF Studio.SchoolLock("error") <> "" THEN
  PRINT "  The policy file "; Studio.SchoolLock("file"); " can't be read: "; Studio.SchoolLock("error")
  PRINT "  Studio keeps every AI feature off, with no password, until it is fixed."
ELSEIF Studio.SchoolLock("policy") = "1" THEN
  PRINT "  This computer's policy turns off: "; Studio.SchoolLock("features")
  PRINT "  (read from "; Studio.SchoolLock("file"); ")"
ELSE
  PRINT "  No School Lock policy on this computer."
END IF

PRINT
PRINT "How hard these passwords are to guess:"
Names(0) = "too short": Names(1) = "weak": Names(2) = "fair": Names(3) = "strong"
Words(0) = "abc12": Words(1) = "123456": Words(2) = "maestra1": Words(3) = "Maestra-2026!"
FOR k = 0 TO 3
  PRINT "  "; Words(k); ": "; Names(Studio.SchoolLockStrength(Words(k)))
NEXT
